This seems to imply that when an element is added to the set, the order of the existing elements should remain unchanged except for the newly added element. However, the condition about null values doesn't make sense in the context of a set, so we'll focus on ensuring that the order of existing elements remains the same.

Given this understanding, the correct assert statement should check that the elements from the given index to the old size minus one have not changed their positions.

Here's the assert statement in the required format:

<code>assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i));</code>

